+---
+type: adr
+status: draft
+entities: [Post]
+related:
+  - app/Http/Controllers/PostController.ts
+  - app/Http/Resources/PostResource.ts
+  - app/Policies/PostPolicy.ts
+  - app/Providers/AuthProvider.ts
+  - routes/web.ts
+  - src/app.ts
+  - db/schema.ts
+  - tests/PostAgentTools.test.ts
+generated: { by: "claude-code/claude-fable-5-1", at: 2026-09-29T19:22:19.565Z }
+---
+
+# Serve agent tools over MCP from the existing post routes
+
+## Context
+
+Authors write with an AI assistant of their own choosing and want it to
+search the blog and draft posts. The assistant reaches the blog over MCP.
+We do not want a chatbot in the blog, a second implementation of search or
+of post creation, or protocol code of our own to maintain.
+
+## Decision
+
+Two existing routes declare `agent` metadata in `routes/web.ts` and become
+the tools. Nothing else defines them: input schema, validation, middleware
+and the policy check are the route's own.
+
+| Tool | Route | Read-only | Who may call |
+|------|-------|-----------|--------------|
+| `posts_search` | `QUERY /posts/search` (`posts.search`) | yes, derived from the method | anyone |
+| `posts_store` | `POST /posts` (`posts.store`) | no | signed-in users, via `PostPolicy.create` |
+
+- Tool names are set with `agent.toolName`, because some assistants drop
+  a tool whose name contains a dot. Route names and paths are unchanged.
+- `@guren/plugin-mcp` serves the tools at `/mcp` (`src/app.ts`). Each tool
+  call re-enters the app as an HTTP request, so it runs the same code path
+  as the website.
+- Callers authenticate with a bearer API token. Tokens live in the
+  `api_tokens` table through `DatabaseApiTokenStore`, configured in
+  `app/Providers/AuthProvider.ts`; only the hash is stored. A token
+  resolves to the full user record, as a session does.
+- The post's author is the calling user. `authorId` is not part of the
+  input schema, so a value sent for it is dropped by validation.
+- A token's `abilities` decide which tools it reaches: `tools:read`,
+  `tool:<name>` or `tools:*`. The store default `['*']` grants no tool.
+
+Ops issue a token from a terminal; the plain text is shown once:
+
+```bash
+bunx guren token:issue --name "Ada's assistant" --user 1 --tools posts_search,posts_store --expires 30d
+bunx guren tool:list    # what the app exposes
+```
+
+## Consequences
+
+- A change to the search or to the "New post" form changes the tool with
+  it. Run `bun run codegen` after touching agent metadata: it regenerates
+  `.guren/agents.gen.ts`.
+- `posts_store` answers the way the form does, with a redirect to the new
+  post, which the assistant reads as `HTTP 303 (Location: /posts/<id>)`.
+  `guren check` warns that the tool advertises no output shape. Giving it
+  one means answering JSON to agents, which we left for when it is needed.
+- The development-only endpoint at `/_guren/mcp` is unrelated: it serves
+  coding tools and is absent in production.
+- Out of scope for now: a page where users manage their own tokens, tools
+  for editing or deleting posts, human approval of tool calls, an audit
+  trail, and rate limits beyond the plugin's per-token defaults.
